---
import basicExampleSource from '../../../../examples/basic.spec.ts?raw'
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro'
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/paths.js'

const nativeExample = `import { defineSuiteCut, renderSuiteCut } from 'suitecut'

const record = defineSuiteCut({
  native: { width: 1920, height: 1080, framesPerSecond: 60 },
  capture: { audio: true },
  output: { manifestPath: '.suitecut/tour.json' },
})

const result = await record('Embedded browser tour', async ({ page, suitecut }) => {
  await page.goto('https://example.com')
  await suitecut.highlight(page.locator('h1'))
  await suitecut.narrate('Welcome to SuiteCut 2.0.')
  await suitecut.checkpoint('Opening screen')
})

await renderSuiteCut({
  manifestPath: result.manifestPath,
  outputPath: '.suitecut/tour.mp4',
})`
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Getting started"
  description="Set up SuiteCut 2.0 with embedded CEF, record a native browser flow, and migrate from Playwright or the beta."
  section="overview"
>
  <h1>Getting started</h1>
  <p>
    SuiteCut 2.0 records and streams with an embedded Chromium browser powered by CEF. The native
    beta is now the default <code>suitecut</code> API. Record a flow with narration, captions, page audio,
    and checkpoints, then render its saved manifest into a video.
  </p>

  <h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Node.js 22 or newer.</li>
    <li>macOS Apple Silicon for the verified native CEF build.</li>
    <li>CMake 3.21+, Ninja, a C++20 compiler, and the pinned CEF and libyuv SDKs.</li>
    <li>FFmpeg and FFprobe, installed with <code>suitecut install</code> or available on PATH.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Linux native builds are unverified. Windows native packaging is not implemented. Use <code
      >suitecut/playwright</code
    > for existing Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit flows on those platforms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock
    label="Terminal"
    code={`npm install https://github.com/skyaara/suitecut/releases/download/v2.0.0/suitecut-2.0.0.tgz
npx suitecut install
npx suitecut doctor`}
  />
  <p>
    Install the 2.0 package from the GitHub release asset above. The package contains the native
    browser source and checksum pins, but no compiled CEF browser. Follow the <a
      href="https://github.com/skyaara/suitecut/blob/main/native/browser/README.md#build"
      >CEF build instructions</a
    > to obtain and verify the pinned dependencies and compile the complete browser bundle. Then set its
    executable path:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    label="Terminal"
    code={`export SUITECUT_NATIVE_EXECUTABLE="/absolute/path/to/suitecut-browser.app/Contents/MacOS/suitecut-browser"`}
  />
  <p>
    Keep the complete <code>.app</code> bundle together. You can also pass
    <code>native.executablePath</code> per recording. A missing browser is an error; SuiteCut never silently
    switches backends. <code>suitecut install</code> installs checksum-pinned media tools, not CEF. Imports
    and recording calls do not download software.
  </p>

  <h2 id="record-a-flow">Record a flow</h2>
  <p>
    Save this as <code>tour.ts</code>. The root recorder launches and closes its primary native
    browser, including after callback errors. Native defaults are 1920 × 1080 at 60 FPS with I420
    capture. Page audio is off by default; the example enables it with <code
      >capture.audio: true</code
    >.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={nativeExample} />
  <p>
    Native locators use strict CSS selectors in the main document. Await application readiness
    explicitly. Role/text locators, iframe traversal, popup flows, and custom Playwright setup
    require the explicit Playwright backend.
  </p>

  <h2 id="run-and-render">Run and render</h2>
  <CodeBlock
    label="Terminal"
    code={`node --experimental-strip-types tour.ts

# Render the saved run again with different output settings:
npx suitecut render \\
  --manifest .suitecut/tour.json \\
  --output .suitecut/tour-4k.mp4 \\
  --width 3840 --height 2160 --fps 60`}
  />
  <p>
    Rendering is separate from browser capture. The manifest keeps authored timing, page selection,
    narration, and checkpoints. Recorded page audio follows source selection and mixes with
    narration. For live output, see <a href={sitePath('/docs/streaming')}>Live streaming</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="playwright-test">Migrating from 1.x and using Playwright Test</h2>
  <p>
    Native beta scripts can change <code>suitecut/beta</code> to <code>suitecut</code>. The beta
    entry point remains an alias. Existing Playwright scripts should change their import:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`import { defineSuiteCut, record } from 'suitecut/playwright'
// Existing Playwright launch, context, capture, and setup options still work.`}
  />
  <p>
    Or keep root <code>record</code> and pass <code>backend: 'playwright'</code> explicitly. The old beta's
    <code>suitecut/stable</code> alias also retains Playwright behavior. Audio flags are boolean in 2.0:
    replace <code>'tab'</code> with <code>true</code> and
    <code>'silent'</code> with <code>false</code>.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    label="Terminal"
    code={`npm install playwright
npx playwright install chromium
# For the optional test runner:
npm install --save-dev @playwright/test`}
  />
  <p>
    <code>suitecut/test</code> and <code>suitecut/reporter</code> keep their existing behavior. Keep Playwright
    trace and video off when SuiteCut owns capture. See the
    <a href={sitePath('/examples')}>Playwright examples</a> for reporter configuration and browser flows.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={basicExampleSource.trim()} />

  <h2 id="render-quality">Render size and frame rate</h2>
  <p>
    Native browser dimensions, device scale, and FPS belong in <code>native</code>.
    <code>capture</code> accepts output <code>size</code>, <code>narrationTailMs</code>, and boolean
    <code>audio</code>. The final renderer defaults to 1920 × 1080 at 30 FPS; request 4K60
    explicitly when using a 4K physical capture.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`import { defineSuiteCut } from 'suitecut'

const record = defineSuiteCut({
  native: {
    width: 1920, height: 1080,
    deviceScaleFactor: 2,
    framesPerSecond: 60,
  },
})`}
  />
</DocsLayout>
